# Dashboard guide

The Dashboard is the main place to create, observe, and control agent Sessions. The hosted Remote Dashboard connects securely to agents running on your device.

## Open the Dashboard

Use [app.pontia.dev](https://app.pontia.dev) and select a registered device. See [Remote access](/docs/remote-access) if the device is not registered yet.

### Local Dashboard

The local Dashboard is available at <http://127.0.0.1:8080/dashboard> and uses the `external_api_token` from `$PONTIA_HOME/config.toml`. Access from another device requires a secure tunnel or forwarding setup.

## Activate a Workspace

A Workspace is the project directory in which an agent runs. Before creating a Session, use [Workspaces](https://app.pontia.dev/workspaces) to browse one of the configured roots and activate the project directory.

Activate directories within your configured Workspace Browser roots. The first initialization uses your home directory as the default root. See [Workspaces](/docs/workspaces) to restrict or change the available roots.

## Start a Session

1. Open [New chat](https://app.pontia.dev/).
2. Select an active Workspace.
3. Select an enabled Agent Client, such as pi, Codex, Claude Agent, or an ACP agent.
4. Describe the job and submit the prompt.

Pontia creates a durable Session and starts the selected Agent Client on your device. The Session remains available in Pontia even when you navigate away from the chat.

## Control active work

The chat page streams the conversation and work steps exposed by the Agent Client. While using a Session, you can:

- send another message when the agent is idle;
- queue input while a supported Agent Client is busy;
- interrupt the current Turn when the Client supports interruption;
- answer tool and permission requests, such as command approvals, when the Client asks for them;
- retry or dismiss Inbox messages whose delivery failed;
- use `/model` to change the model for later Turns when the Client supports model changes;
- type `@` to find files and directories in the active Workspace;
- attach files with the **+** button in the composer, up to 1 GiB each;
- edit an eligible earlier user message to branch from that point in the native conversation history.

The Inbox tracks submitted messages waiting for delivery or queued by an Agent Client.

## Shared files

An agent can share a file from its Session by running `pontia send-file PATH`. The file appears as a card at the end of the Turn, where you can preview or download it. Open **Shared files** in the composer menu to list every file shared in the Session. Pontia reads the file from the device when you download it, so a file that was moved or deleted is no longer available.

## Chat commands

Type `/` in the composer to see commands available in the current context:

| Command | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `/new` | Start a new Session, keeping the current Workspace when possible |
| `/rename` | Rename the current Session |
| `/model` | Choose a model for subsequent Turns, when supported |
| `/compact` | Summarize older context while the Session is idle, when supported |
| `/exit` | End Pontia's active control of the current Session |

`/exit` ends Pontia's control of the Session. The Agent Client manages the lifecycle and storage of its native conversation.

## Keyboard shortcuts

Chat pages provide these shortcuts:

| Shortcut | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `Alt+J` / `Alt+K` | Move to the next or previous active chat |
| `Alt+1` … `Alt+9` | Open an active chat by sidebar position |
| `Alt+N` | Open New chat |
| `Alt+L` | Focus the composer |
| `Alt+?` | Show the shortcut reference |
| `Ctrl+B` (`Cmd+B` on macOS) | Toggle the sidebar |

## Organize Sessions

Use a Session's action menu to rename, pin, archive, or end it. The **Sessions** page separates active, archived, and pinned Sessions. Archiving removes a Session from the active list without deleting its recorded control state.

The chat header also shows available metadata such as Workspace, Git branch and status, model, context usage, and Client. Fields appear only when the selected Client reports them.

For service or connection errors, continue with [Troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting).
